SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T205000
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Thu. Dec. 10 · Call 7:30 PM · 8:10 PM–8:50 PM · Robinson
  Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 7:30 PM: dancers must 
 be checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 7:15 PM. BA: Call Tim
 e is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minut
 es before Call Time.\nACT II Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair 
 and Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHA
 NGE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal 
 are the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/
 1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP
  for Hot Chocolate: Spanish Hot Chocolate — Costume (you provide): Pin
 k Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Pointe Sho
 es w/ ribbons & elastics (clean\, quiet\, unpancacked)\; Makeup: Full St
 age Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction She
 et:\n•  Apply foundation and powder matching skintone\n•  Ligh
 t skin tone eye shadow over entire eye\n•  Dark brown eye shadow ov
 er crease\n•  Medium brown eye shadow blended over brown\n•  B
 lack fake eyelashes (note: apply mascara to own lashes before applicatio
 n of fake lashes)\n•  Apply eyeliner after lashes dry\n•  Blus
 h on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed
  out in the stage lights)\n•  Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, 
 hairline\n•  Use a brow pencil (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrow
 s\n•  Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh ton
 e tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• 
  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to del
 icate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of c
 ostume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n•
   Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes
  by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on the floor whil
 e in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launde
 r any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage make-up while in c
 ostume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on cos
 tume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of spray perfume o
 r cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garment not assigned 
 to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or beverage while 
 in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not remove costumes
  from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n•  Remove 
 all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n
 •  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•  Comply ful
 ly with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•
   Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or anything that may 
 damage or stain costumes.
