  Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 2:45 PM: dancers must 
 be checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 2:30 PM. BA: Call Tim
 e is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minut
 es before Call Time.\nACT II Cast B Performance.\nAll Casts are called u
 nless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedule\, th
 e weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Master: ht
 tps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kk
 w24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP for Hot Chocolate: Spanish Hot Cho
 colate — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone cami
 sole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Pointe Shoes w/ ribbons & elastics (clean\, q
 uiet\, unpancacked)\; Makeup: Full Stage Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Pa
 rt\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n•  Apply foundation and p
 owder matching skintone\n•  Light skin tone eye shadow over entire 
 eye\n•  Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n•  Medium brown eye
  shadow blended over brown\n•  Black fake eyelashes (note: apply ma
 scara to own lashes before application of fake lashes)\n•  Apply ey
 eliner after lashes dry\n•  Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply p
 lenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n•  
 Brown or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n•  Use a brow pencil
  (or eyeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n•  Red or Dark Red Lipstick
 \nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoe
 s.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care wh
 ile changing to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly not
 ify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume damage at the point of disco
 very\, no matter how significant\n•  Never throw costumes or access
 ories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  R
 efrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attemp
 t to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n• 
  Never apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take great care to
  refrain from smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n•  Re
 frain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n• 
  Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not hand
 le or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of 
 water\n•  Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms
  or from the theater\n•  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head 
 pieces and wigs following their use\n•  Return all headpieces to th
 eir assigned bags\n•  Comply fully with any and all updates to Ball
 et Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\,
  colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
